# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Zheyong Fan et al. (2021). Neuroevolution machine learning potentials: Combining high accuracy and low cost in atomistic simulations and application to heat transport.
#   Physical review. B./Physical review. B. doi:10.1103/physrevb.104.104309  arXiv:2107.08119v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2107.08119v2 (sha256 333a4306052b43c7...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 214 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/fan2021.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the NEP method (introduced here) fitted to general-purpose
# silicon, 2D silicene and bulk PbTe, and the GAP-SOAP, MTP and DP
# comparison potentials the authors trained on the silicene and PbTe sets
# (Table II), plus the general-silicon force RMSEs of NEP and DP (text).
# Virial RMSEs, the thermal-conductivity results and the regularisation
# study (App. D, figures) are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-fan2021 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Fan et al. (2021): neuroevolution machine-learning potentials (NEP) and heat transport" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-fan2021 .

entity:article-fan2021 a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
    schema:sameAs <https://doi.org/10.1103/physrevb.104.104309> ;
    schema:datePublished "2021"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:name "Neuroevolution machine learning potentials: Combining high accuracy and low cost in atomistic simulations and application to heat transport" ;
    schema:author <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2253-8210> ,
        <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5126-4928> ,
        <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4562-535X> ,
        entity:person-Wang-fan2021 ,
        entity:person-Song-fan2021 ,
        <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9870-0467> ,
        entity:person-Chen-fan2021 ,
        entity:person-AlaNissila-fan2021 .

