###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# MD speed was measured on 8,000-atom (silicon, PbTe) and 6,000-atom
# (silicene) cells: NEP in gpumd on one Nvidia Tesla V100 reaches above
# 1e7 atom-steps per second, more than an order of magnitude faster than
# compressed DP on the same GPU; GAP-SOAP and MTP ran on 72 Intel Xeon-Gold
# 6240 cores (Fig. 4). The NEP timing is recorded as inferenceHardware on
# the general-silicon result. Training cost is proportional to N_pop x
# N_gen; no times are given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - NEP is introduced as a neural-network potential with a Chebyshev/Legendre descriptor trained by an evolution strategy; no derivation from a registry method is stated.
# - The RMSEs of Table II and of the general-silicon set are computed on the training data (Sec. III C), so their role is training. Virial RMSEs (meV/atom) have no metric property in the schema and are not encoded.
# - Fig. 4 prints speeds (from 2,000 to 13,000,000 atom-steps per second) next to bars; which value belongs to which potential and material is not reliably readable from the text layer, so only the 'above 1e7' statement for NEP is kept.
# - The GAP silicene and MTP PbTe inputs (App. B 2, B 3) are not encoded. NEP descriptor orders (n_max, l_max) and the population size are given in Table I but have no hyperparameter individual.
# - The DFT settings of the general-silicon data set are those of Ref. [47] (not restated here).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/fan2021.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

